    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "x-api-key",
              "value": "YOUR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
            },
            {
              "name": "anthropic-version",
              "value": "2023-06-01"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 300,\n  \"system\": \"You are ThreadKeep, an intelligent work conversation analyst for Indian professionals. Your job: Analyse any work message and extract ALL meaningful work signals. Handle Hinglish, informal language, abbreviations, and voice note transcriptions naturally.\\n\\nClassify every message into one or more of these types:\\n- TASK: Something that needs to be done\\n- DECISION: Something agreed upon or finalised\\n- COMMITMENT: Someone personally promising to do something\\n- BLOCKER: Something stopping progress\\n- MEETING: A meeting or sync being scheduled\\n- FYI: Important information to remember\\n\\nAlways respond with ONLY a JSON object. No explanation. No extra text.\\n\\nIMPORTANT SOURCE RULES:\\n- Every message starts with a source prefix like: 'slack | sender: Name | message: ...' or 'Gmail (your_personal_account) | sender: Name | message: ...' or 'Gmail (your.email@example.com) | sender: Name | message: ...' or 'whatsapp | message: ...'\\n- For Gmail messages: use the EXACT source label from the prefix (e.g. 'Gmail (your_personal_account)' or 'Gmail (your.email@example.com)') as the source field\\n- For Slack messages: use 'slack' as source\\n- For WhatsApp messages: use 'whatsapp' as source\\n- Extract the sender name from the prefix for original_sender field\\n\\nReturn this structure:\\n{\\n  signals: [\\n    {\\n      type: TASK|DECISION|COMMITMENT|BLOCKER|MEETING|FYI,\\n      summary: clear 1 line summary in English,\\n      person: name or unspecified,\\n      deadline: date/time or null,\\n      priority: high|medium|low,\\n      confidence: high|medium|low\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  source: use exact source label from prefix,\\n  original_sender: name or null\\n}\\n\\nHinglish rules: kal tak = by tomorrow, aaj EOD = by end of today, jaldi = urgent, main le leta hoon = commitment, ho jayega = will be done, ruk gaya hai = blocker.\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"{{ \n  ($json.real_name ? 'slack | sender: ' + $json.real_name + ' | message: ' + $('Slack').item.json.body.event.text \n  : ($json.snippet ? $json.source_label + ' | sender: ' + ($json.From ? $json.From.replace(/<.*>/g, '').trim() : 'unknown') + ' | message: ' + $json.snippet \n  : 'whatsapp | sender: ' + $json.body.senderData.senderName + ' | message: ' + $json.body.messageData.textMessageData.textMessage)) \n}}\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        304,
        16
      ],
      "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000007",
      "name": "Claude LLM"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Step 1: Get Claude's raw response text\nconst rawText = $input.first().json.content[0].text;\n\n// Step 2: Strip the ```json ``` backticks Claude adds\nconst cleanText = rawText.replace(/```json/g, '').replace(/```/g, '').trim();\n\n// Step 3: Parse it into real JSON\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(cleanText);\n\n// Step 4: Create IST timestamp\nconst now = new Date();\nconst istTime = new Date(now.getTime() + (5.5 * 60 * 60 * 1000));\nconst day = istTime.getUTCDate().toString().padStart(2, '0');\nconst months = ['Jan','Feb','Mar','Apr','May','Jun','Jul','Aug','Sep','Oct','Nov','Dec'];\nconst month = months[istTime.getUTCMonth()];\nconst year = istTime.getUTCFullYear();\nlet hours = istTime.getUTCHours();\nconst minutes = istTime.getUTCMinutes().toString().padStart(2, '0');\nconst ampm = hours >= 12 ? 'PM' : 'AM';\nhours = hours % 12 || 12;\nconst timestamp = `${day} ${month} ${year}, ${hours}:${minutes} ${ampm} IST`;\n\n// Step 5: Loop through each signal and create one output row per signal\nconst rows = parsed.signals.map(signal => {\n  return {\n    json: {\n      type: signal.type,\n      summary: signal.summary,\n      person: signal.person || 'unspecified',\n      deadline: signal.deadline || 'not mentioned',\n      priority: signal.priority,\n      confidence: signal.confidence,\n      source: parsed.source || 'whatsapp',\n      original_sender: parsed.original_sender || 'unknown',\n      timestamp: timestamp,\n      status: 'open',           \n      id: 'xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx'.replace(/[xy]/g,         function(c) {\n      var r = Math.random() * 16 | 0;\n      return (c === 'x' ? r : (r & 0x3 | 0x8)).toString(16);\n      })\n    }\n  };\n});\n\n// Step 6: Return all rows\nreturn rows;"
      },
